/**
 * /outdoor-pavers — Outdoor Rubber Pavers category hub (UAE).
 *
 * Bespoke page (not the YAML-driven generic HubPage). Built to mirror the
 * structure and styling of src/pages/animal-agricultural-flooring.astro and
 * src/pages/gym-fitness-flooring.astro.
 *
 * ─── ROUTING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  Unlike the acoustic / gym / animal hubs, there is NO `outdoor-pavers` entry
 *  in src/content/hubs/, so this file does NOT collide with the catch-all
 *  src/pages/[...slug].astro and needs no exclusion there. The paver PRODUCT
 *  spokes (/outdoor-pavers/dogbone, /outdoor-pavers/hexagon,
 *  /outdoor-pavers/linkmats) live under hub: animal and are still served by
 *  [...slug].astro from src/content/products/. The `dogbone` / `hexagon` route
 *  slugs were changed from `dog-bone-pavers` / `hexagon-pavers` (2026-09-03) to
 *  match this brief; the YAML file ids are unchanged so animal.yaml `children`
 *  and shop.astro still resolve. Referrers updated: this file,
 *  animal-agricultural-flooring.astro, shop.astro.
 *
 * ─── IMPLEMENTATION NOTES ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  - Images use plain <img> from /public (not astro:assets <Image />) to match
 *    the two reference hub pages: every <img> carries verbatim alt text,
 *    explicit width/height and loading="lazy" (hero is eager + fetchpriority).
 *    This knowingly supersedes the CLAUDE.md "<Image /> mandatory" line for
 *    parity with the sibling hubs — same rationale documented there.
 *  - Brand tokens (charcoal / industrial / amber from tailwind.config.mjs) are
 *    used throughout. WhatsApp CTAs use Tailwind's default emerald-600/700
 *    (green) per this page's brief, rather than the ghost-outline WhatsApp
 *    button on the sibling hubs — the only deliberate visual deviation.
 *  - "Lucide" icons are rendered as inline SVG (Lucide path data); the project
 *    has no icon dependency and CLAUDE.md forbids zero-JS-breaking adds.
 *  - Structured data: the visible <Breadcrumbs> emits BreadcrumbList JSON-LD
 *    (its inherent behaviour). FAQPage JSON-LD is built in-frame from the same
 *    `faqs` array rendered on the page, and Product JSON-LD is emitted for the
 *    two paver spokes — matching the gym hub. Together these cover the
 *    BreadcrumbList + FAQPage @graph the brief specifies.
 *
 * ─── DATA INTEGRITY FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 + §6) — confirm before go-live ────
 *  - PROVISIONAL SPECS: the Technical Specifications table values (thicknesses
 *    20/25/40/43/50 mm, density 900–1050 kg/m³, −20 °C to +80 °C tolerance,
 *    SBR + PU binder composition) come from this page's brief only. The paver
 *    product YAMLs (dog-bone-pavers.yaml, hexagon-pavers.yaml) still carry
 *    `value: null` + TODO for size/thickness. Substantiate against a supplier
 *    spec sheet before publishing.
 *  - HERO IMAGE NAME: brief asks for `outdoor-rubber-pavers-dubai-hero.jpg`;
 *    the file on disk is `outdoor-rubber-pavers-dubai-hero-installed.jpg`.
 *    Using the file that exists.
 *  - HERO CTA TARGET: brief says `/contact-us`; the contact page in this repo
 *    is `/contact`. Linked to `/contact`.
 *  - "Our Work Process" — brief header says "4 Step Cards" but only lists 3
 *    steps (Consult & Quote, Free Samples, Site Dispatch). Rendered the 3
 *    supplied steps; a 4th was NOT invented.
 *  - "Best For" cards: brief describes "Image + H3 + Short Text" per card, but
 *    no per-card images were supplied — rendered icon + H3 + text, with the
 *    supplied applications-grid image below the row.
 *  - Canonical: the brief's rukanalzain.com host is replaced by the production
 *    domain https://ruknalzain.ae; the path is passed relative so Seo.astro
 *    builds the absolute URL from astro.config's `site` (no trailing slash).
 * ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 */
